# Lobium patch apply order (quilt). One patch path per line, applied top to bottom.
#
# ARCHITECTURE
# Almost all Lobium logic lives in ADDED files under //components/lobium_fp/ (staged from lobium/src/
# by build.ps1 / build.sh). An added directory never conflicts on an upstream rebase, so the patches
# below are only the MINIMAL hook points into existing Chromium files - each one routes a surface
# through lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current() and falls back to the real host value when the config is
# absent. Keeping them tiny is what makes tracking Chrome stable within days feasible.
#
# ONE PATCH PER CONCERN. Every hunk belongs to exactly one patch. That is not cosmetic:
#   * `patch --forward` reports a duplicated hunk as "previously applied" and exits non-zero, which
#     silently breaks a whole-series apply;
#   * a duplicated hunk rejects in two patches at once on rebase, and neither quilt nor git can tell
#     you which concern actually broke.
# ci/validation/patch-series.test.mjs enforces this: no hunk body may appear in two patches.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. Patches that hook the same upstream FILE at different places are cut against the
# tree as it exists after the earlier ones applied, so their context can contain Lobium lines. The
# constrained chains are noted inline below.
#
# Status of every hook, with its exact file and line, is in ../hooks.md. The diffs are the source of
# truth; hooks.md explains why each one exists.

# =================================================================================================
# Native product shell
# =================================================================================================
# =================================================================================================
# Core: build wiring, capability contract, config transport
# =================================================================================================
# Registers the added //components/lobium_fp module in the build graph: blink core, blink common,
# blink modules, components/embedder_support:user_agent and content/renderer.
core/build-gn.patch
# --lobium-fingerprint-capabilities: the executable prints its versioned contract before browser
# startup, so the sidecar probes the exact binary it will spawn instead of trusting a filename.
# Must precede every capability-gated surface. Keep in sync with
# packages/engine-runner/src/lobium-capabilities.ts.
core/capability-contract.patch
# Transport only: the browser reads --lobium-fp-config once and forwards base64 --lobium-fp-data to
# every renderer (workers included). Every surface below is a separate patch.
core/config-channel.patch
# navigator.* + User-Agent header + Sec-CH-UA, in all contexts including workers.
core/navigator-ua-ch.patch

# =================================================================================================
# Fingerprint surfaces (the native moat)
# =================================================================================================
# Canvas 2D + OffscreenCanvas readback farbling (seeds.canvas).
fingerprint/canvas-farbling.patch
# WebGL vendor/renderer + scalar caps + pixel farbling (seeds.webgl).
# CHAIN: webgl-surfaces -> host-gpu-profile -> webgl-runtime-safety, all in
# webgl_rendering_context_base.cc. The later two are cut against the earlier ones and cannot apply
# to a pristine tree; never validate them in isolation.
fingerprint/webgl-surfaces.patch
# Deep WebGL: version / shadingLanguageVersion / extensions / shaderPrecision. Confirmed necessary
# by battle-test on real GPUs - the extension set and precision leaked the host while
# UNMASKED_RENDERER was already spoofed.
fingerprint/host-gpu-profile.patch
# Never advertise a capability the active GL backend cannot execute.
fingerprint/webgl-runtime-safety.patch
# Closes two call sequences that routed AROUND the hooks above: a no-op PACK_ROW_LENGTH that switched
# readPixels farbling off, and a WebGL1 extension list collapsing on a WebGL2 context. Last in the
# chain and cut against all three; verified with lobium/chain-delta.mjs.
fingerprint/webgl-bypass-closures.patch
# WebGL2-only limits: the uniform/varying COMPONENT counts, which ANGLE derives as exactly 4x the
# WebGL1 VECTOR limits the patches above already spoof. Separate file, separate TU
# (webgl2_rendering_context_base.cc), so it is outside the three-patch chain above.
fingerprint/webgl2-surfaces.patch
# navigator.gpu adapter identity, derived from the same GPU the WebGL renderer names. Must not be
# skipped when WebGL is spoofed: an unhooked WebGPU adapter reports the real card next to a spoofed
# WebGL renderer, and the mismatch is a stronger signal than either surface alone.
fingerprint/webgpu-adapter.patch
# Web Audio farbling (seeds.audio): OfflineAudioContext result + AnalyserNode float AND byte paths.
fingerprint/audio-context.patch
# The upstream sample taps a page can read BEFORE the farbled offline result:
# AudioWorkletProcessor.process(inputs) and ScriptProcessorNode.onaudioprocess inputBuffer. Gated to
# offline contexts so realtime DSP is untouched.
fingerprint/audio-worklet-tap.patch
# Persona screen geometry + colour depth + DPR, through window.devicePixelRatio AND the CSS
# media-query path so matchMedia agrees with the getter.
fingerprint/screen-dpr.patch
# matchMedia('(device-width/height)') must agree with screen.width/height (CreepJS Screen lie).
# CHAIN: after screen-dpr; both hook media_values.cc.
fingerprint/media-values-device-size.patch
# navigator.webdriver, answered in Blink rather than by --disable-blink-features. The flag kept it
# false but raised Chromium's "unsupported command-line flag" infobar and named itself on
# chrome://version - two tells bought to hide one.
fingerprint/navigator-webdriver.patch
# navigator.language(s) in all contexts + configured geolocation after a normal permission grant +
# ICU locale applied before Blink/V8 init.
fingerprint/locale-geolocation.patch
# clientRects farbling (seeds.clientRects).
fingerprint/client-rects.patch
# mediaDevices.enumerateDevices from policy.mediaDevices.
fingerprint/media-devices.patch
# Android persona parity: suppress the desktop PDF plugin surface when the config declares uaMobile.
fingerprint/mobile-persona.patch
# Four observably distinct WebRTC policies; proxy_only is relay-only, disabled rejects
# RTCPeerConnection.
fingerprint/webrtc-policy.patch
# The persona timezone applied inside the engine. NOT redundant with the launcher's TZ variable: TZ
# is POSIX-only and ICU ignores it on Windows, so the env route silently did nothing there. Hooked at
# OnTimeZoneChange because the browser's TimeZoneMonitor overwrites anything adopted earlier.
fingerprint/native-timezone.patch
# Windows font-set isolation through DirectWrite (FindFamily, MatchUniqueFont, Local Font Access) plus
# the font-pack sideload. Windows-only by nature: Linux reaches the same isolation through the
# launcher's per-profile FONTCONFIG_FILE, which is not a property of the binary.
fingerprint/windows-font-isolation.patch

