# Present on disk but deliberately NOT in the series:
#   branding/suppress-sandbox-infobar.patch - only needed for --no-sandbox dev runs.
#   branding/device-frame.patch - the Android phone/tablet workspace behind the real WebContents.
#     REMOVED FROM THE SERIES 2026-08-21 because it does not link on Linux, which is the only
#     platform it targets. Its own note claimed it "applies cleanly and changes nothing"; that is
#     true only on Windows, where every hook is excluded by #if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX). On Linux the
#     hooks DO compile, they reference LobiumDeviceFrameView, and its implementation file is in no
#     GN target - so `chrome` fails at the final link with seven undefined symbols:
#         ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: LobiumDeviceFrameView::IsEnabled()   (+6 more)
#     Measured on 152.0.7977.42 after a full 8h21m compile: 56069 of 56070 steps succeeded and the
#     link was the single failure. Finishing the feature needs lobium_device_frame_view.cc added to
#     a GN target AND content/{public/browser,browser/devtools}/lobium_device_emulation.* carried in
#     lobium/src/ (they exist only as untracked files on one build host today). Until then it must
#     stay out, or no Linux engine can be produced. See ../hooks.md "device frame".
